    <h2>Ironman 70.3 — half distance</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">A 1.9 km swim, 90 km ride and a half marathon. It's where most triathletes step up to long distance: it demands real volume, but it still fits around a working life. Plans run 19 to 20 weeks, with first-timer, intermediate and advanced versions, plus variants that add gym work.</p>

    <h2>Ironman 140.6 — full distance</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">A 3.8 km swim, 180 km ride and a marathon. Here the limiter stops being speed and becomes durability: holding power and pace after hours of load. Plans run 22 to 24 weeks, because the aerobic adaptation this distance asks for can't be rushed. If it's your first full, start with the first-timer plan — it's built to get you to the line intact, not fast.</p>
  </div>
</section>

